Expected elements: MISSING — a timeline or scrubber expressing position within the trace.

Everything else on the must-show list is here: provenance banner above the identity bar (badge, `aztec` slug, four producer sentences), a slim single-row identity bar with a chain-targeted exit, truncated hash, `Partial`, block, four stepping groups in both directions, the `128 / 1315` readout and the phase rail; Code positioned at line 32; Call Trace and Event Log as one tabbed region with Call Trace open and seven frames; Values as its own pane below, not a tab; the Transaction pane. No forbidden item. But the identity bar carries no timeline and no scrubber at this viewport — between the last button group (x≈655) and the readout (x≈672) there is nothing, and position within 1,315 steps is expressed only as a numeric fraction. That is finding 1, it is P1, and the rating is capped at 4.

As a density surface the filled rows are strong — tabular ACIR column, marked changed values, excellent inline value chips — but the 900px budget is spent badly. 178px (20%) goes above the first pane to a banner whose prose sits in a 580px measure inside a 1440px band; all three panes are consequently sliced mid-glyph at y=900; and the call-trace region wastes 123px while the Values pane below it is truncated.

Highest-priority fixes after restoring a position graphic: give the Values pane the height the call-trace region is not using, and set the banner's prose at the band's own width.

Rating: 4/10

